abstract: >-
  Data, code, and materials to reproduce every figure and table in the
  paper and its supplementary online material. The study is a
  lab-in-the-field experiment with 64 local leaders and 384 villagers
  across 32 villages in the Ohangwena region of northern Namibia,
  testing whether conditional payments for democratic governance crowd
  in or crowd out democratic behaviour among leaders who manage
  communal natural resources. Data are de-identified; see the README
  section "Data anonymization" for what was removed and why.
keywords:
  - conditional payments
  - democratic governance
  - lab-in-the-field experiment
  - local leaders
  - environmental governance
  - crowding out
  - Namibia
  - replication package
